Now,
\[\frac{2^k}{5^{2^k} + 1} = \frac{2^k}{5^{2^k} + 1} \cdot \frac{5^{2^k} - 1}{5^{2^k} - 1} = \frac{2^k(5^{2^k} - 1)}{5^{2^{k + 1}} - 1}
\]
is a telescoping series. We have
\begin{align*}
\left(\sum_{k \ge 1} \frac{2^k}{5^{2^k} + 1}\right) - \left(\sum_{k \ge 1} \frac{2^k}{5^{2^{k+1}} + 1}\right) &= \frac{1}{5 + 1}
\end{align*> <end think> <answer> \boxed{\frac{1}{6}} </end answer>

